  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This 2022 Springer Nature book chapter has already attracted visible public attention and an early scholarly citation. The record also shows a teaching-adoption signal through a YouTube video that explicitly links to the work, suggesting that its unusual design topic has moved beyond the page into broader discussion.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">\u201cSmelly Shoes\u2014An Opportunity for Shoe Rack Re-Design\u201d by Vikash Kumar and Sarthak Mittal, published in the <em>Design science and innovation</em> series, presents a small but distinctive scholarly footprint. The chapter sits at the intersection of engineering and everyday design, with concepts centered on clothing, racks, and applied engineering. Its topic is practical and accessible, which likely helps explain why it has drawn attention beyond specialist audiences.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest signal in the record is public visibility: the work has been referenced in newsfeed-based attention sources and appears to have generated active discussion. That kind of uptake indicates that the chapter\u2019s idea resonated as a notable example of design research with an immediately legible real-world problem. The available record also includes a reader-facing signal through the cover metadata, reinforcing its presence as a discoverable book chapter in the Springer Nature catalogue.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Scholarly uptake is still early but present. OpenAlex records one citation, and the citing landscape points to a 2025 BMJ article that references the chapter in the context of an Ig Nobel awards discussion. That citation does not by itself establish sustained academic influence, but it does show the work being taken up in later scholarly commentary and connected to a wider conversation about inventive, unusual, or humorous research.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">There is also a clear teaching-adoption signal: a YouTube video explicitly links the paper in its metadata and description. Combined with the book\u2019s placement in a design-oriented series and the availability of a WorldCat holding record, this suggests the chapter has been discoverable to both academic and general audiences. Overall, the evidence shows a work with strong visibility and modest but real scholarly reach, with its impact currently expressed more through public discussion and educational reuse than through a large citation trail.</p>",
